  "description": "A continuous process in biocatalysis or industrial chemistry refers to a method where the reaction operates continuously, with substrates constantly supplied into the system and products continuously removed during the process.
A description for a batch reaction could be “The system/reactor operates continuously with the continuous supply and removal of reactants".
."
